    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170">

                <pb facs="0170" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.01/416: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador to the Greek
                        Government in Exile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacVeagh</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at Cairo</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-18T00:00:00-04:00">December 18,
                            1943—midnight</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Greek [Series] 63. A complete reversal of British policy toward the Greek King
                    seems indicated in your Greek 128, December 12, 10 a.m. and 130, December 14, 10
                        a.m.<anchor n="62" xml:id="d170-f1"/> Please report any obtainable
                    information as to reasons for this change.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
